      "math_academy_id": "q-96864",
      "sequence_position": 1,
      "problem": "Approximate the value of $z$ such that $P(Z\\le z)=0.2900$ using interval bisection.\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.05\\,$ | $\\,0.06\\,$ | $\\,0.07\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,-0.5\\,$ | $\\,0.2912\\,$ | $\\,0.2877\\,$ | $\\,0.2843\\,$ |\n| $\\,-0.4\\,$ | $\\,0.3264\\,$ | $\\,0.3228\\,$ | $\\,0.3192\\,$ |\n| $\\,-0.3\\,$ | $\\,0.3632\\,$ | $\\,0.3594\\,$ | $\\,0.3557\\,$ |",
      "worked_solution": "First, we find the two numbers in the table that $0.2900$ lies between. These numbers are $0.2877$ and $0.2912.$ So, we have the following inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0.2877 & <0.2900<0.2912\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above inequality in terms of $Φ,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Φ(-0.56) & <Φ(z)<Φ(-0.55).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, using interval bisection, we can approximate $z$ as\n\n$$\nz≈\\frac{-0.56+(-0.55)}{2}=-0.555.\n$$",
